1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,070
Why was the Ambassador particularly lucky?
大使为什么特别幸运？

2
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:15,720
Why was the Ambassador particularly lucky?
大使为什么特别幸运？

3
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:24,250
When the Ambassador of Escalopia returned home for lunch, his wife got a shock.
当埃斯卡罗比亚国的大使回家吃午饭时，他的妻子大吃一惊。

4
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,970
He looked pale and his clothes were in a frightful state.
他面色苍白，衣服也弄得不成样子。

5
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:33,100
'What has happened?' she asked.
“出了什么事？”她问。

6
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:36,440
'How did your clothes get into such a mess?'
“你的衣服怎么搞得这么狼狈？”

7
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:41,900
'A fire extinguisher my dear,' answered the Ambassador drily.
“灭火器弄的，亲爱的，”大使冷冷地回答说。

8
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:47,120
'University students set the Embassy on fire this morning.'
“今天上午大学生们放火烧了大使馆。”

9
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:53,220
'Good heavens!' exclaimed his wife.
“天哪！”他妻子惊叫起来。

10
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:55,330
'And where were you at the time?'
“当时你在哪儿？”

11
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:01,400
'I was in my office as usual,' answered the Ambassador.
“我跟平常一样在办公室里，”大使回答说。

12
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:04,200
'The fire broke out in the basement.
“火是在地下室起的。

13
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:10,200
I went down immediately, of course, and that fool, Horst,
我当然马上就下去了，可那个笨蛋霍斯特

14
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:12,860
aimed a fire extinguisher at me.
把灭火器对准了我。

15
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:15,260
He thought I was on fire.
他以为我身上着火了。

16
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:20,010
I must definitely get that fellow posted.'
我一定要把那家伙调走。”

17
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:24,830
The Ambassador's wife went on asking questions,
大使夫人继续问下去，

18
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:30,380
when she suddenly noticed a big hole in her husband's hat.
这时她突然发现丈夫的帽子上有个大洞。

19
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:36,730
'And how can you explain that?' she asked.
“这个你怎么解释？”她问。

20
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,650
'Oh, that,' said the Ambassador.
“哦，这个，”大使说。

21
00:01:42,050 --> 00:01:44,720
'Someone fired a shot through my office window.
“有人从我的办公室窗户开了一枪。

22
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:46,730
Accurate, don't you think?
打得很准，你不觉得吗？

23
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:50,510
Fortunately, I wasn't wearing it at the time.
幸好我当时没戴帽子。

24
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:55,580
If I had been, I would not have been able to get home for lunch.'
要是戴着的话，我就回不来吃午饭了。”
